WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:08.013
A detection prediction needs both a label and a spatial region. Box coordinates first require a

00:00:08.013 --> 00:00:15.827
convention: corner format, coordinate origin and whether endpoints are continuous or inclusive integer pixel positions. Inconsistent

00:00:15.827 --> 00:00:17.780
conventions change computed areas.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:24.683
Each box has width two and height two. We use continuous coordinates, so no inclusive-pixel plus-one

00:00:24.683 --> 00:00:25.880
correction is added.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:33.200
Intersection width is clamped at zero when the boxes are separated. Negative intersection area has no

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:34.050
geometric meaning.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:40.247
How far can the box move before intersection becomes zero? Pause here and make a prediction

00:00:40.247 --> 00:00:40.957
before continuing.

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:49.877
Adding both areas counts the shared region twice. Subtract it once to obtain the union. For

00:00:49.877 --> 00:00:55.247
our starting inputs, Intersection area: 2. Union area: 6. IoU: 0.33333.

00:00:55.767 --> 00:01:02.447
The ratio is scale-free for valid boxes with nonzero union. Zero means no overlap; one means

00:01:02.447 --> 00:01:04.117
the two boxes coincide.

00:01:04.633 --> 00:01:11.983
Compute geometry before applying an IoU threshold, and document the matching rules used in detection evaluation.

